Treat SUBZERO as a portfolio of deterministic gate-fabric generators, measured .mno artifacts, and structurally tested archetypes—not as proven runtime intelligence unless evidence shows it. Study existing Commons revenue/payment-ready lanes to avoid duplicate offers or founder-slot collisions.

Design a maximum-overdrive but honest revenue architecture across: RIGHT NOW, 10 days, 30 days, 90 days, 180 days, 1 year, 2 years. Include:
• many noncompeting paths (productized service, paid validation, tooling, catalog, licensing, R&D contracts, workshops, partnerships, recurring support);
• price ladder, conversion path, prerequisites, variable cost, founder time, and cash-collection mechanics without private banking data;
• open-source/commercial boundary and defensibility;
• channel strategy and specific customer evidence needed before scaling;
• portfolio dependencies/collisions;
• a cold-eyed ranking by time-to-cash, probability, upside, and proof burden.
Do not collapse everything into one startup/app. Do not overclaim revenue or runtime performance. No outreach or transactions.
